$ enola cluster --help
exit: 2
--- stdout
--- stderr
Usage: enola cluster init [--dry-run] [dir]

init writes a cluster config for a folder that holds several git repositories.
Run `enola cluster init --help`.

Examples:
  # See the config it would write for a folder of repositories
  enola cluster init --dry-run ~/src

  # Write it
  enola cluster init ~/src

  # Index every repository in it as one linked graph
  enola --generate ~/src/cluster.yaml

See also: enola help cluster init, enola help coverage
